A||||3||Tonker||Mountain View CA Tourist Attractions?||||5||
Z||000000||Tonker||07-13-2001||02:47 PM||||I'm on a business trip to Mountain View next week, are there any good places, Fiero Related or otherwise, to visit in the area? <P>------------------<BR>Black '86 Fiero GT.<BR>ICQ: 7813479||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tonker||07-13-2001||03:11 PM||||Come to think of it, anyone know how long it would take to get to San Francisco from Mountain View? Is it feasible to go sightseeing there in an evening?||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||07-13-2001||03:25 PM||||Mountain View is in close proximity to San Francisco. I recommend taking BART rather then driving to save a LOT of hassle. Of course, you could go the other way and go to San Jose and see where all this techno-stuff took root. Lots of cool museums in San Jose like the Rosicrucian Museum (all kinds of neat ancient Egyptian stuff, mummies and sarcophagi).<P>How does an Okie know all this? I grew up in San Jose and spent most of my life in the bay area.<P>Oh, one more thing. San Francisco is freakin COLD this time of year. Don't go sportin shorts down to Fisherman's Wharf during the summer.<P>And the only thing Mountain View has noteworthy is NASA/Ames research center, Shoreline Park, and Mustard Mike's hot dog stands. (Mustard Mike's Polish dogs are the shiznit!)||||reg||1
Z||000003||EdsB52||07-14-2001||05:08 PM||||I lived on Tyrella ave, Mountain View in the 70's and then again in the early 80's. It's right near the Navy base. There was absolutely nothing there at that time, but a beautiful place anyway. I would check out Palo Alto, which is 10 miles North of Mountain View. Stanford University resides there as well and is another beautiful city. Lots of touristy stuff, but I don't know how much Fiero related stuff is there. Have fun.||||reg||1
